    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d867">

                <pb facs="1167" n="1047" xml:id="pg1047"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/864½: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on Special Mission in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-24T18:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 25—12:35
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>72. President Zayas has just informed me that, assuming the loan is approved, he
                    desires service of Governor Harding<anchor n="55" xml:id="d867-f1"/> in
                    connection with the forthcoming audit and upon terms and conditions mentioned by
                    me. He hopes that he may report on November 1st, or as soon thereafter as
                    practicable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crowder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d867-f1" n="55" xml:id="d867-f1-content">
                <p>W. P. G. Harding, Governor of the Federal Reserve Board.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
